    },
    {
      "id": "qXmcHVPn",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3252.804328831222,
      "y": -1884.0254026121784,
      "width": 1050.6369378559734,
      "height": 339.6842286967428,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2G",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 721010472,
      "version": 476,
      "versionNonce": 2055388200,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1773245089238,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "=========================================================================================\nTECHNOLOGY TYPE    | OLD \"SHARED\" STRATEGY            | MODERN \"INTEGRATED\"\nSTRATEGY\n=========================================================================================\nMongoDB (Document)   | All apps write to one \"Common\"        | Database-per-Service; sync via \n                             | collection. (High Coupling)               | Change Streams/Kafka.\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nVector DB (LLM)        | Every AI app queries one giant        | RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation)\n                            | central Vector store.                     | via specialized Service APIs.\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGraph DB                | One central \"Master Graph\" used      | Domain-specific graphs linked \n                            | by the whole company.                   | through a Data Mesh/Federation.\n=========================================================================================",
      "fontSize": 20.90364484287648,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "=========================================================================================\nTECHNOLOGY TYPE    | OLD \"SHARED\" STRATEGY            | MODERN \"INTEGRATED\" STRATEGY\n=========================================================================================\nMongoDB (Document)   | All apps write to one \"Common\"        | Database-per-Service; sync via \n                             | collection. (High Coupling)               | Change Streams/Kafka.\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nVector DB (LLM)        | Every AI app queries one giant        | RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) \n                            | central Vector store.                     | via specialized Service APIs.\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGraph DB                | One central \"Master Graph\" used      | Domain-specific graphs linked \n                            | by the whole company.                   | through a Data Mesh/Federation.\n=========================================================================================",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "YC09JwBp",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -258.49977182708653,
      "y": -1205.7430800995555,
      "width": 198.76742553710938,
      "height": 54.78448885749412,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2H",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 77205032,
      "version": 158,
      "versionNonce": 209653592,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1773245101259,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "OLD - IBM MQ, \nTIBCO MQ, MSMQ",
      "fontSize": 21.913795542997647,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "OLD - IBM MQ, \nTIBCO MQ, MSMQ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "5obOxg0s",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1744.588001578274,
      "y": -1344.258923857174,
      "width": 1023.0545654296875,
      "height": 391.943340803934,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2I",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 463209048,
      "version": 253,
      "versionNonce": 1177089832,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1773245089238,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "=========================================================================================\nPATTERN TYPE       | EIP CLASSIC EXAMPLE (2003)       | MODERN EQUIVALENT (2026)\n=========================================================================================\nMessage Broker     | IBM MQ (WebSphere MQ), TIBCO,    | Confluent Cloud (Kafka), Redpanda, \n                         | MSMQ (Microsoft Message Queue)   | Amazon SNS/SQS, Azure Service Bus\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMessage Bus        | Enterprise Service Bus (ESB)          | Event Mesh (Solace), NATS JetStream, \n                        | (e.g., MuleSoft, Oracle ESB)           | Google Cloud Pub/Sub\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPublish-Subscribe  | JMS (Java Message Service)         | Apache Kafka, Apache Pulsar, \n                       | Topics, RabbitMQ (AMQP)           | WarpStream\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMessage Router    | Custom Java/C# Code, Camel,      | Serverless Functions (AWS Lambda), \n                       | BizTalk Server                         | KSQLDB, Apache Flink\n=========================================================================================",
      "fontSize": 20.90364484287648,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "=========================================================================================\nPATTERN TYPE       | EIP CLASSIC EXAMPLE (2003)       | MODERN EQUIVALENT (2026)\n=========================================================================================\nMessage Broker     | IBM MQ (WebSphere MQ), TIBCO,    | Confluent Cloud (Kafka), Redpanda, \n                         | MSMQ (Microsoft Message Queue)   | Amazon SNS/SQS, Azure Service Bus\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMessage Bus        | Enterprise Service Bus (ESB)          | Event Mesh (Solace), NATS JetStream, \n                        | (e.g., MuleSoft, Oracle ESB)           | Google Cloud Pub/Sub\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPublish-Subscribe  | JMS (Java Message Service)         | Apache Kafka, Apache Pulsar, \n                       | Topics, RabbitMQ (AMQP)           | WarpStream\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMessage Router    | Custom Java/C# Code, Camel,      | Serverless Functions (AWS Lambda), \n                       | BizTalk Server                         | KSQLDB, Apache Flink\n=========================================================================================",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "WXtaQYsf",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3036.5794358674357,
      "y": -1333.8016219690512,
      "width": 1023.0545654296875,
      "height": 470.3320089647208,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2J",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2112687704,
      "version": 319,
      "versionNonce": 1464848936,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1773245089238,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "=========================================================================================\nSTRATEGY PILLAR    | CLASSIC EIP (2003)               | MODERN CLOUD-NATIVE (2026)\n=========================================================================================\nLogic Placement    | \"Smart Pipes\": Logic lived in             | \"Dumb Pipes\": Logic lives in the \n                       | the Middleware (ESB).                    | Microservices/Consumers.\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMessage Life       | Transient: Read and delete              | Durable: Persistent logs/streams \n                       | (Destructive Read).                       | that allow for \"Replay.\"\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPrimary Goal       | Reliability: Ensuring a command          | Agility: Allowing many systems to \n                       | is delivered and executed.               | react to an \"Event\" in real-time.\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nScale Direction    | Vertical: High-spec servers                | Horizontal: Distributed clusters \n                       | with manual failover.                      | with automatic partitioning.\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCoupling Type      | Temporal: Sender and Receiver        | Decoupled: Producers don't care \n                       | often need to be \"active.\"            | who (or how many) consume data.\n=========================================================================================",
      "fontSize": 20.90364484287648,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "=========================================================================================\nSTRATEGY PILLAR    | CLASSIC EIP (2003)               | MODERN CLOUD-NATIVE (2026)\n=========================================================================================\nLogic Placement    | \"Smart Pipes\": Logic lived in             | \"Dumb Pipes\": Logic lives in the \n                       | the Middleware (ESB).                    | Microservices/Consumers.\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMessage Life       | Transient: Read and delete              | Durable: Persistent logs/streams \n                       | (Destructive Read).                       | that allow for \"Replay.\"\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPrimary Goal       | Reliability: Ensuring a command          | Agility: Allowing many systems to \n                       | is delivered and executed.               | react to an \"Event\" in real-time.\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nScale Direction    | Vertical: High-spec servers                | Horizontal: Distributed clusters \n                       | with manual failover.                      | with automatic partitioning.\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCoupling Type      | Temporal: Sender and Receiver        | Decoupled: Producers don't care \n                       | often need to be \"active.\"            | who (or how many) consume data.\n=========================================================================================",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "cW7NTwBw",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1724.900447237994,
      "y": -705.3314020831194,
      "width": 1023.0545654296875,
      "height": 313.5546726431472,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2K",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1160597080,
      "version": 231,
      "versionNonce": 1961053480,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1773245089238,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "=========================================================================================\nERA / TECH         | DATA STRATEGY            | PROCESSING MODEL     | LATENCY\n=========================================================================================\nEIP (2003)         | Messaging: Small packets | Point-to-Point       | Milliseconds\nLegacy Integration | (IBM MQ, TIBCO)          | (Request-Response)   | (Small volume)\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHADOOP (2010s)     | Big Data: Data at Rest   | Batch Processing     | Hours / Days\n\"The Data Lake\"    | (HDFS, MapReduce)        | (Scan entire disk)   | (Huge volume)\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSTREAMING (2026)   | Data in Motion: Events   | Stream Processing    | Milliseconds\n\"The Data River\"   | (Kafka, Flink, Pulsar)   | (Continuous/Stateful)| (Huge volume)\n=========================================================================================",
      "fontSize": 20.90364484287648,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "=========================================================================================\nERA / TECH         | DATA STRATEGY            | PROCESSING MODEL     | LATENCY\n=========================================================================================\nEIP (2003)         | Messaging: Small packets | Point-to-Point       | Milliseconds\nLegacy Integration | (IBM MQ, TIBCO)          | (Request-Response)   | (Small volume)\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHADOOP (2010s)     | Big Data: Data at Rest   | Batch Processing     | Hours / Days\n\"The Data Lake\"    | (HDFS, MapReduce)        | (Scan entire disk)   | (Huge volume)\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSTREAMING (2026)   | Data in Motion: Events   | Stream Processing    | Milliseconds\n\"The Data River\"   | (Kafka, Flink, Pulsar)   | (Continuous/Stateful)| (Huge volume)\n=========================================================================================",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "wXLV8mL1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1721.95152206177,
      "y": -740.7185041978096,
      "width": 491.83929443359375,
      "height": 26.1295560535956,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
